sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-takahashii-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila takahashii Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 2.362 µm (Pass 1 field render) faithfully reproduces Drosophila takahashii morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-takahashii-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila takahashii specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-takahashii-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-takahashii-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_takahashii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila takahashii; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 diffusion-driven instability and a finite critical wavelength | Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics with a cubic autocatalytic term | Murray 1981 wavelength set by the diffusion scale | Tanaka, Barmina and Kopp 2009 and Kopp 2011 on sex-comb diversification | Atallah et al. 2014 on Drosophila suzukii and its close relatives; reconstructed_in_script: Parameters a=0.162, b=1.247, Du=0.042744, Dv=0.971570 placing λ_c at 2.362 µm | Explicit Euler on a periodic 12-wavelength chart and the radial-FFT wavelength | Dispersion Pearson/KS, Dv sweep, and equal-diffusion ablation; transfer_boundary: 2.362e-06 m is the campaign detail-scale assignment (log10=-5.627), not a quoted takahashii ocellus measurement | The suzukii → takahashii → teissieri order is chronoseries index 37/41 at 0 Ma, not an anagenetic fossil series; does_not_claim: That a wet-lab paper reports 2.362 µm for a D. takahashii ocellus | That D. takahashii carries the D. suzukii apical wing spot | That the Pass 1 Otsu contour is a usable body outline]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1039/a702602a>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0807875106>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2013.2840>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1525-142x.2011.00507.x> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-takahashii-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-takahashii-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

